From 2a4faf169aa5a2cc54494875799765bdd66a5ed1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FNGarvin <184324400+FNGarvin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:30:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Add MSE stream-to-disk dump feature

Right-click "Dump Media Stream..." on a playing MSE video/audio element
dumps every attached SourceBuffer's raw appended bytes, in order, to its
own file per track (MseStreamDumper), bypassing site-level anti-tamper
and download-blocking JS since the capture point sits below it. Content
sandbox must be disabled (MOZ_DISABLE_CONTENT_SANDBOX=1) for file writes
to succeed; writes happen off the main thread via a dedicated TaskQueue.
DRM/EME content is excluded since decrypted bytes never reach this layer.
